<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Echizen Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Echizen was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast, now the northern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukui-prefecture">Fukui Prefecture</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> it was ruled by the Asakura clan from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ichijodani">Ichijōdani</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> destroyed them in 1573. Under the Tokugawa it formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukui">Fukui</a> domain of the Matsudaira, a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a>'s family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/echizen-province.jpg" alt="Echizen Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Echizen.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
